 "note": "Babble voice data (audio/audio_babble.gd plans, audio/synth/babble_synth.gd renders). A caption becomes a run of short syllables shaped by the text, the mood and the fighter's voice; laughs and grunts punctuate it. The syllable bank is tiny (about 60 clips of about 100 ms per voice at 12 kHz) and is played with pitch changes, so a line costs a few play calls and no synthesis at run time. v2: moods for every node of Narrative's mood graph (docs/narrative/dialogue-director.md), a voice-specific mood for the Anti-hero's cracked facade, and three display styles: caption, thought (sparse, breathy, quiet and muffled, no laughs) and shout.",
